  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "OpenTelemetry 2026 status snapshot",
      "items": [
        "Lifecycle is assigned per specification component, signal, protocol, SDK, and Collector component; a stable signal or API does not imply that every language implementation or Collector component is stable. The status page lists tracing API/SDK/OTLP stable, metrics API and data model/protocol stable with SDK maturity mixed, baggage stable, logs specification/bridge API/SDK/protocol stable, and profiles protocol in development. Check the implementation-specific status before selecting a language library or Collector component."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/status/",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/status/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Prometheus 3.8 and 3.9 native histogram milestones",
      "items": [
        "Prometheus v3.8.0 marks native histograms stable, but in v3 scraping remains opt-in with scrape_native_histograms; in v3.8 the old feature flag only sets that configuration default, while from v3.9 the flag is a no-op. Remote-write transmission separately requires send_native_histograms. Do not infer end-to-end enablement from stability."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/specs/native_histograms/",
        "https://prometheus.io/download/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "OpenTelemetry Collector Contrib v0.165.1 (latest release checked 2026-11-20); OTTL v1 milestone v0.164.0",
      "items": [
        "OTTL v1 became stable for traces, metrics, and logs starting with opentelemetry-collector-contrib v0.164.0. This stability promise covers the OTTL language, not every Collector processor or component; the transform processor was still described as a separate promotion effort in the announcement."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/releases",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2026/ottl-v1/",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/collector/transforming-telemetry/"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "accuracyFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Prometheus native histograms are stable starting with v3.8.0, but stability does not enable collection or forwarding. In v3 scraping requires scrape_native_histograms; in v3.8 the legacy native-histograms feature flag only changes that setting's default, and from v3.9 it is a no-op. Remote write separately requires send_native_histograms. Prometheus v4 documentation states both settings default true.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/specs/native_histograms/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "OpenTelemetry maturity is component-specific. The current specification status summary reports tracing API/SDK/OTLP stable; metrics API and data model/protocol stable with SDK maturity mixed; baggage stable; logging specification, bridge API, SDK and protocol stable, with event semantic convention support in the bridge marked experimental; profiles protocol is in development. Language SDKs and Collector components vary independently.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/status/",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/status/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "OTTL v1 is stable for traces, metrics and logs beginning with opentelemetry-collector-contrib v0.164.0. This language stability does not make the transform processor or all OTel Collector components stable.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2026/ottl-v1/",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/collector/transforming-telemetry/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "OpenTelemetry Profiles are an alpha/development signal in the supplied specification status snapshot. Profiles can complement metrics, logs and traces by showing sampled resource consumption; do not present profiles protocol or broad cross-language profile instrumentation as stable.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/profiles/",
        "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/concepts/signals/profiles/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "Prometheus experimental PromQL functions require the promql-experimental-functions feature flag and can change. In particular, histogram_quantiles, info, integral, double_exponential_smoothing, time-boundary functions, sort_by_label variants, and experimental over-time functions must not be presented as universally available stable syntax.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/functions/",
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/operators/",
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/feature_flags/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "The current PromQL function reference also includes experimental, feature-flagged integral, max_of, and min_of functions; circular trigonometric functions use radians, hyperbolic functions use dimensionless numeric values, deg and rad convert angle units, and pi returns a scalar. start_timestamp has a separate use-start-timestamps feature gate.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/functions/",
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/feature_flags/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "Current PromQL also includes vector matching modifiers on/ignoring/group_left/group_right, comparison bool, aggregation operators including experimental limitk and limit_ratio, and optional binary fill modifiers gated by promql-binop-fill-modifiers. Histogram trim operators </ and >/ operate on native histograms with scalar thresholds. Consult the deployed Prometheus version and feature flags; latest documentation can describe features newer than an installed server.",
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/operators/",
        "https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/feature_flags/"
      ]
    }
  ],
